T) makes equipment for semiconductor and display production. The ledger shows $29.0 billion in trailing-year revenue and $21.5 billion in trailing-year expenses. It also shows $6.5 billion in reported debt and $7.0 billion in total committed money.","debt":"The filings report $6.5 billion of debt. Total committed money is $7.0 billion, including $6.5 billion of debt and $813 million of leases. Purchases are listed at $0 million.","wall":"The company reports $13.3 billion due in the next 5 years, plus $1.1 billion due in years 5 to 10 and $1.2 billion beyond 10 years. Against this, the ledger shows $1.0 billion of future revenue in the next 5 years and $2.6 billion of deferred revenue.","flags_note":"The filings also report purchase obligations outside debt and lease balances, including $10.6 billion at October 26, 2025. They show changes in credit and commercial-paper commitments, a $253 million BIS settlement, and a past $2.2 billion Kokusai Electric acquisition commitment that is not reported later."}}